       "description": "Every thermal rate coefficient of RADM2 at the urban noon: T = 298 K, M = 2.46e19 molec/cm3, RH 0.55 box state, against RCONST(22:156) of the WRF-conform KPP Update_RCONST (radm2_Update_Rconst.f90 generated by KPP 2.1 from radm2.eqn, compiled real64 with gfortran 13.3 in the WRF build container; standalone box driver data/eqwefic/chem_build/driver, dump /projects/illinois/eng/cee/ctessum/ctessum/data/eqwefic/dumps/radm2/box_urban_noon.json). Pointwise, no time step. Expected agreement is binary64 round-off (the same double-precision arithmetic in both), so the tolerance is the CLAUDE.md double-precision contract rel 1e-9; the single-precision literals of radm2.eqn (.20946e0, .78084, -2.3) are bound as their binary64 values so no rounding residual remains. The one exception is k_R043 (N2O5 + aerosol water, rc_n2o5), which WRF evaluates in SINGLE precision in kpp_mechd_ibu_radm2.inc: tolerance rel 1e-6 (measured residual ~1e-7). There is no WRF-Chem run behind these states; they are typical mixing-ratio boxes (make_states.py).",
       "parameter_overrides": {
         "T": 298.0,
         "M_air": 2.4623522626293244e+19,
         "RH": 0.55,
         "j_no2": 0.0085,
         "j_o31d": 3.2e-05,
         "j_o33p": 0.00042,
         "j_hno2": 0.0017,
         "j_hno3": 6.5e-07,
