     {
       "id": "box_urban_night_rate_constants",
       "description": "Every thermal rate coefficient of RADM2 at the urban night: T = 283 K, M = 2.59e19, RH 0.90 box state, against RCONST(22:156) of the WRF-conform KPP Update_RCONST (radm2_Update_Rconst.f90 generated by KPP 2.1 from radm2.eqn, compiled real64 with gfortran 13.3 in the WRF build container; standalone box driver data/eqwefic/chem_build/driver, dump /projects/illinois/eng/cee/ctessum/ctessum/data/eqwefic/dumps/radm2/box_urban_night.json). Pointwise, no time step. Expected agreement is binary64 round-off (the same double-precision arithmetic in both), so the tolerance is the CLAUDE.md double-precision contract rel 1e-9; the single-precision literals of radm2.eqn (.20946e0, .78084, -2.3) are bound as their binary64 values so no rounding residual remains. The one exception is k_R043 (N2O5 + aerosol water, rc_n2o5), which WRF evaluates in SINGLE precision in kpp_mechd_ibu_radm2.inc: tolerance rel 1e-6 (measured residual ~1e-7). There is no WRF-Chem run behind these states; they are typical mixing-ratio boxes (make_states.py).",
