     {
       "id": "wrfchem_scm_midtrop_rate_constants",
       "description": "Every thermal rate coefficient of RADM2 at a real WRF-Chem state: the mid-troposphere level k = 45 (T = 254.674 K, p = 490.1 hPa, M = 1.3939e19 molec/cm3, RH = 0.156, late-afternoon TUV/Madronich photolysis) of the first chemistry call of the idealized single-column WRF-Chem run described below, against RCONST(22:156) written by the fork's chem/KPP/inc/radm2/kpp_mechd_*_radm2.inc hooks straight after Update_Rconst (dump /projects/illinois/eng/cee/ctessum/ctessum/data/eqwefic/dumps/radm2_wrf/esm_dump_radm2_kpp_1.json, level k = 45). Run: WRF v4.8.0 em_scm_xy ideal case, 1999-10-22 19:00 UTC, 59 levels, chem_opt = 101 (RADM2 KPP), phot_opt = 1 (Madronich TUV), emiss_opt = 0, chem_in_opt = 0 (species from the built-in idealized profiles of chem/module_input_chem_data.F), no dry deposition; ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem. Pointwise, no time step. Unlike the three box regimes this state comes from a full WRF-Chem column: T, C_M and the photolysis frequencies are whatever the model's own meteorology and radiative transfer produced, and T = 254.7 K sits well outside the 283-298 K of the box regimes, so the Arrhenius and Troe forms are exercised far from them. WRF is built single precision (RWORDSIZE = 4), but the KPP interface promotes t_phy, rho_phy and the photolysis rates to KIND = dp = real64 before Update_Rconst, so every rate law is evaluated in double there exactly as in the box driver; the dumped inputs are bound here as their exact binary64 values, hence the same rel 1e-9 double-precision contract as the box regimes (largest measured residual over the 134 double-precision coefficients: 6.2e-16, one ulp -- they all still pass at rel 1e-15). The exception is again k_R043 (N2O5 + aerosol water): WRF evaluates rc_n2o5 in single precision from a single-precision relative humidity that the interface does not carry out of the loop, so RH is reconstructed here from the dumped qv, p_phy and T with the float32 formula of kpp_mechd_ibu_radm2.inc; the reconstruction reproduces the dumped rc_n2o5 to 3.7e-8 relative, so its tolerance is rel 1e-6. Cross-check: at this state all 156 RCONST entries of the WRF-Chem run agree bit-for-bit with the standalone real64 KPP box driver (data/eqwefic/chem_build/driver) fed the same T, C_M, C_H2O, RH and jv, which is what ties this regime to the other three.",
