   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "box_urban_noon_tendencies",
     "description": "Instantaneous net production rate of all 59 variable species at the urban noon (T 298 K, RH 0.55, clear-sky noon photolysis) box state, against Vdot from radm2_Fun of the standalone WRF-Chem RADM2 KPP box driver (data/eqwefic/chem_build/driver, real64, KPP-generated code from chem/KPP/mechanisms/radm2 of WRF v4.8.0 with WRFUserRateLaws; dump dumps/radm2/box_urban_noon.json). This is the instantaneous-derivative shape PLAN.md section 6 asks for: each d<SPC>_dt is an observed written D(RADM2.<SPC>, t), which esm-spec section 7.4 resolves to the tendency the reaction system already derives, so asserting it at time 0 evaluates the mechanism right-hand side at the given state and pins the whole stoichiometric matrix and every rate law independently of any integrator. The environment (T, M, H2O, RH, photolysis) is set through the same scoped parameter_overrides as the matching trajectory test. Measured agreement with the Fortran (Rust CLI, real64 both sides): 102 of the 177 assertions across the three regimes are BIT-IDENTICAL to KPP, the largest residual anywhere is 9.5e-7 relative (dALD_dt, rural morning) and every other species is within 3.9e-8. That residual is summation-order rounding amplified by cancellation, not a stoichiometric difference: ALD sums 35 terms whose net is 1.1 % of the largest of them, and reconstructing the budget from this document's own stoichiometry times the dump's reaction rates A reproduces the esm value rather than the Fortran one. The tolerance is held at rel 1e-5 rather than tightened to that residual because evaluation ORDER differs between bindings, so a tolerance tuned to one binding's rounding would not hold in the others; every error class this test exists to catch -- a wrong stoichiometric coefficient, a misbound rate law -- moves a tendency by O(1), not by 1e-6.",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1
     },
     "tolerance": {
      "rel": 1e-05
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "RADM2.O3": 1477411357577.5947,
      "RADM2.H2O2": 24623522626.293247,
      "RADM2.NO": 492470452525.86487,
      "RADM2.NO2": 984940905051.7297,
