    {
     "id": "box_urban_night_trajectory",
     "description": "Trajectory of the urban night (T 283 K, RH 0.90, no photolysis) box state integrated by the KPP Rosenbrock (Rodas3, ICNTRL(3)=4 as WRF) solver of the standalone WRF-Chem RADM2 box driver (data/eqwefic/chem_build/driver, real64, KPP-generated code from chem/KPP/mechanisms/radm2 of WRF v4.8.0 with WRFUserRateLaws; RTOL 1e-9, ATOL 1e-3 molec/cm3): the concentrations of 12 species after 60, 300 and 1800 s. There is NO WRF-Chem reference run; the initial state is a typical mixing-ratio profile (make_states.py). Tolerance rel 1e-5 is the solver-to-solver agreement expected between the KPP Rosenbrock at rtol 1e-9 and the binding integrator; the rate coefficients themselves are pinned to 1e-9 by the RADM2RateConstants tests. The environment (T, M, RH, photolysis) is set through scoped parameter_overrides into RADM2RateConstants, whose observeds every reaction rate references. Run for the first time on 2026-09-12, after EarthSciAST #251 (issue #206) taught the Rust CLI to execute reaction_systems inline tests; measured agreement with the KPP Rosenbrock reference is better than rel 1e-7 on every one of the 12 species at all three output times, the tightest being the fast NO3/N2O5 night pair between 1e-8 and 1e-7. The document declares `solver.abstol` 1e-3 molec/cm^3 (the box driver's own ATOL): the runner default of 1e-6 is meaningless for a state carried in molec/cm^3 and collapses the step size to zero at t ~ 1e-14 s in both daylight regimes.",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1800
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "O3": 518573126688.0133,
      "H2O2": 25928656334.400665,
      "NO": 51857312668.80133,
